Description: Tools for exploring, visualizing, and comparing classification decision boundaries
    in R. Provides a unified interface for fitting classifiers and rendering 2D decision
    boundary plots, with support for 2D slice visualization (fixing non-plotted dimensions at
    reference values) and projection-based visualization for high-dimensional data (including
    PCA and tour projections from the 'tourr' package). Supports native R classifiers,
    tidymodels workflows, and custom user-supplied models via a flexible adapter system.
    Includes an interactive Shiny application ('explorapp') for visual exploration, data
    simulation, drawing, model comparison, probability surfaces, and reproducible exports.
